@startuml hld-05a_window_containment
title HLD-05a — Window containment, HIGH VIEW (UML **class diagram**)\nA filled diamond is UML composition: the part has no life outside its whole.\nWhich widget instance sits in which slot is HLD-05b.
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide circle
hide empty members

class MainWindow <<shell>> #LightGray
class Sidebar <<shell>> #LightGray {
  entries derived from
  registry.screens()
}
class QStackedWidget <<shell>> #LightGray {
  one page visible at a time
  (PresenterManager)
}
class ModalHost <<shell>> #LightGray {
  opened and closed
  by the current page
}

abstract class Surface {
  +surface_id : String
  +accepts : Place [1..*]
}

class WelcomeSurface <<shell-owned>> #LightGray
class TradingSurface <<shell-owned>> #LightGray
class DevBoardSurface <<shell-owned>> #LightGray {
  {gated by dev.mode at boot}
}
class SettingsSurface <<shell-owned>> #LightGray
class BacktestScreen <<owned by backtesting>> #Wheat {
  accepts = {RAIL, MODAL}
}
class DataManagementScreen <<owned by market_data>> #Wheat

class PageShell {
  +slot(place : Place) : Container
}

interface IContributionRegistry {
  +screens() : ScreenContribution [*]
  +for_place(surface_id, place) : ContributionDescriptor [*]
}

MainWindow *-- "1" Sidebar
MainWindow *-- "1" QStackedWidget
MainWindow *-- "1" ModalHost
QStackedWidget *-- "1..*" Surface
Surface *-- "1" PageShell

Surface <|-- WelcomeSurface
Surface <|-- TradingSurface
Surface <|-- DevBoardSurface
Surface <|-- SettingsSurface
Surface <|-- BacktestScreen
Surface <|-- DataManagementScreen

Sidebar ..> IContributionRegistry : <<use>>\nscreens()
PageShell ..> IContributionRegistry : <<use>>\nfor_place(surface_id, place)\nfor each slot it owns
PageShell ..> ModalHost : <<use>>\nopens

note right of PageShell
  **A page never invents layout (§4.6).** Every slot a `PageShell` owns is a
  literal of the `Place` enumeration (HLD-03a); a module can only ask for
  "my widget in `<surface_id>`.`<place>`", and the slot resolves the geometry.
end note

note bottom of Sidebar
  The sidebar is **not** a `Place`: it is derived entirely from `SCREEN`
  contributions, and nothing else may be contributed into it.
end note

note bottom of BacktestScreen
  A module-owned screen is an ordinary `Surface` subclass. It differs only in who
  declares it and in the value of `accepts` — which is how `strategy` places a
  modal on `BacktestScreen` without `backtesting` importing `strategy`.
end note
@enduml
